    <string name="config_external_input_title">External keyboard/mouse</string>
    <string name="config_external_input_message">Android already supports external keyboards and mice natively — no package or driver needs to be installed inside Kairos.\n\n• USB/OTG: connect an OTG cable to the device port and plug in the keyboard/mouse — Android detects it automatically.\n\n• Bluetooth: System settings → Bluetooth → Pair device, follow the normal pairing process for the keyboard/mouse.\n\nOnce connected, it works throughout the app — including the terminal (shortcuts, arrow keys, Ctrl/Alt, mouse scroll) with no extra setup.</string>
